menu "SolarYou application"

choice SOLARYOU_RUNTIME_MODE
    prompt "Runtime mode"
    default SOLARYOU_RUNTIME_SENSOR_DASHBOARD_TEST
    help
        Choose whether this build is only reading the real sensors and sending
        dashboard telemetry, or whether it may also command the two servos.

config SOLARYOU_RUNTIME_SENSOR_DASHBOARD_TEST
    bool "Sensor/dashboard test (motor outputs disabled)"
    help
        This is a safe test mode for checking the UART connection. The BNO085
        provides the pitch and roll readings. It also checks the light sensors,
        but a problem with them will not stop the IMU data from being sent.
        The INA219 is optional for now because power data is not connected
        yet. The servos stay off in this mode.

config SOLARYOU_RUNTIME_FULL_CONTROL
    bool "Full integration (motor outputs enabled)"
    help
        Initializes the servos and runs the full light-tracking and PID motor
        control path. This mode should be selected once all hardware
        connections and GPIO assignments have been verified.

endchoice

endmenu
